11. Calls upon all parties to facilitate the safe and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance, and to cooperate fully with the United Nations and humanitarian actors, including by simplifying administrative procedures and ensuring timely issuance of visas and permits;

12. Reaffirms its strong commitment to the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of Syria, stresses that all humanitarian operations in Syria should be conducted with full respect for the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of Syria and in accordance with the guiding principles of humanitarian emergency assistance, and calls upon all parties to refrain from actions that undermine the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Syria;

13. Reaffirms its support for the full implementation of resolution 2254 (2015) and for the United Nations-facilitated political process in Syria, and stresses that a sustainable political settlement is essential to ending the humanitarian crisis;

14. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

